(*
PulseNodeDK.ns — the Task 8 nRF52840-DK acceptance-bar node. Identical to the
Task 7 native_sim gate (PulseNode.ns) EXCEPT it does NOT call `gpio fire: 13`:
on the DK the one edge comes from a PHYSICAL button press (BUTTON1 / P0.11),
routed by the Zephyr GPIO ISR in ../src/main.c -> gpio_target_fire(13) -> the
same (chan_id, handle_idx) this node registered via `gpio pin: 13 ...`. Baking
the sim `gpio fire:` in here would post a pulse at boot and print `observed
done` with NO button press, defeating the whole point of the hardware bar — so
it is removed. The C-owned pump loop then blocks (pulse_pump: K_FOREVER) until
the button is pressed.

Baked into the DK boot image with (run from the nsl-tuvm repo):
  python3 tools/ns_compile_oevm.py \
    ~/workspace/tuvm/zephyr/PulseNodeDK.ns \
    ~/workspace/tuvm/src/solidified_image.c

Same two dialect deviations as PulseNode.ns, for the same reasons:
  - `[ ... ] repeat` is unsupported; use `[ true ] whileTrue:`.
  - post the String 'done' (not Symbol #done) so `printString` yields
    `observed done`, not `observed #done`.
*)
class PulseNodeDK packageUsing: manifest = () (
  public main: platform args: args = (
    | space alert gpio |
    space:: platform space.
    alert:: space channel: 'sensor/alert'.
    alert whenever: '' do: [ :e | ('observed ' , e printString) out ].
    gpio:: platform gpio.
    gpio pin: 13 edge: #rising post: 'done' on: alert.
    (* no `gpio fire:` — a physical BUTTON1 edge drives the one pulse *)
    [ true ] whileTrue: [ platform pumpEvents. space drain ]
  )
) : (
)
